                    <occupation>Lawyer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>There is a Joshua Evans, described as a bookseller who was a member of
                            the Westminister Committee in 1819. But there is also a lawyer who
                            defended a number of radicals, including John Cam Hobhouse in February
                            1820, and Richard Carlile in 1831. It also looks as
                            if he has some connection with Gresham college, and may have been on the
                            Committee for the appointment of lecturers.</p>
